        {
          "id": 1644395533,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hi John,\nThanks for your review.  I've read  Bug 15494 and don't understand the\nregression you mentioned. That report concerned an issue where \"[TCP\nsegment of a reassembled PDU] followed a [Reassembled in <frame>]. My\nchange just places the same info that's in the Packet Detail (e.g.,\n\"[Reassembled PDU in frame: 149]\" on the Packet List line. Can you please\nelaborate on your concern about testing first_pdu? If it concerns the first\nbytes of the next PDU I could test for and display that info but as Guy\nsaid, \" the fact that it also happens to be the first TCP segment of the\nPDU following that PDU is not of interest.\"",
          "author": {
            "id": 6901460,
            "username": "cturney111",
            "public_email": "cturney111@gmail.com",
            "name": "Cal Turney",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/6901460/avatar.png?v=1782345656",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/cturney111"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-11-11T21:22:52.901Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-11-11T21:22:52.901Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 262295618,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "commit_id": null,
