        {
          "id": 1644397931,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "The current code tests `first_pdu` and only places the information in `COL_INFO` if it is the `first_pdu`. You moved it, but you also got rid of that test. That means that you *will* add to `COL_INFO` if the frame contains the first TCP segment of a second or later PDU, even when there was a first PDU completely dissected with a subdissector.\n\nThat is, your change will cause bug #15494 to reappear. Below is a screenshot where I checked out your MR, compiled it, and dissected the file attached in bug #15494\n\n![MR bad](/uploads/0d55bafac1cdff03473b6d6d63513877/image.png)\n\nHere is what it looks like with the current master:\n\n![image](/uploads/9168040796d60672c3b2f7472bb731bb/image.png)\n\n(There is both DICOM-level reassembly and TCP-level reassembly.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
